---
globs:
  - "src/**/*.ts"
---
Failures raised in `src/` are `AppError` from `src/errors/appError.ts` or a subclass (`WebhookParseError`, `StaleHeadPushError`), with a closed `{domain, kind}` pair from `APP_ERROR_KINDS` in `src/errors/appErrorCodes.ts` (`{ domain: "config", kind: "invalid_enum" }`; adding one is an edit to that table, never a free-form string), whose derived `code` `<domain>.<kind>` is the persisted and logged string (`config.invalid_enum`, `ask.sensitive_path_blocked`, `triage.stale_head_push`), a technical `message`, JSON-safe `context` (never secrets or repo content), and `cause` when wrapping. Callers branch on `code` or `instanceof`, never on message text. `AppError.message` and `context` never reach a PR comment, check, reaction, or status; PR-facing copy is a plain-English settings constant. Log with `errorLogFields` / `serializeAppError`; `sanitizeErrorForTelemetry` guards evlog and analytics. `throw new Error(...)` is only for programmer invariants no caller branches on (`src/agent/executio
